        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x.$ Then  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$  gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | ${e}^{2}$ | ${e}^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{2}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {u}^{2}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (16-4) \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$",
